# Build/package outputs. `packaging/` is deliberately NOT here: it holds the
# Windows build recipe (build_windows.ps1, archive_release.ps1, the PyInstaller
# spec, prepare_default_model.py), which is source, not output. It was ignored
# until 2026-08-02, which meant a fresh clone of a Windows-distributed tool had
# no way to produce a build. `*.spec` is scoped to the repo root so PyInstaller's
# generated specs stay ignored while packaging/jav-trans-web.spec is tracked.
build/
dist/
/*.spec
*.7z
*.7z.*
*.zip
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.*

# Claude Code project instructions are local to this workspace.
CLAUDE.md

# Local MCP/infra deployment notes (not published)
grok-search-mcp部署文档.md

# pyproject.toml is the source of truth; `uv sync` is the documented install.
# (requirements.txt was removed 2026-07-31 - it duplicated the dependency list
# but omitted the [tool.uv.sources] cu132 pin, so following it produced a CPU
# torch. Kept at agents/rm/20260731_170000_requirements_txt_superseded_by_pyproject/.)
#
# uv.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. The release ships it and installs with
# `uv sync --frozen`, so an untracked lockfile means a fresh clone cannot build
# the release anyone is actually running. It holds nothing private - package
# names, versions, hashes, and index URLs.
